### Define and call tools with generateText

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/03-ai-sdk-core/15-tools-and-tool-calling.mdx

Defines a function tool using the tool helper with a Zod input schema and execute function, then passes it to generateText. Uses isStepCount in stopWhen to manage multi-step tool calls.

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';
import { generateText, tool, isStepCount } from 'ai';
__PROVIDER_IMPORT__;

const result = await generateText({
  model: __MODEL__,
  tools: {
    weather: tool({
      description: 'Get the weather in a location',
      inputSchema: z.object({
        location: z.string().describe('The location to get the weather for'),
      }),
      execute: async ({ location }) => ({
        location,
        temperature: 72 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 21) - 10,
      }),
    }),
  },
  stopWhen: isStepCount(5),
  prompt: 'What is the weather in San Francisco?',
});
```

--------------------------------

### Enable multi-step tool calls with generateText and stopWhen

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/cookbook/05-node/53-call-tools-multiple-steps.mdx

Configures generateText with stopWhen set to isStepCount(5) to allow the model to execute tools across multiple steps until the stopping condition is met.

```ts
import { generateText, tool, isStepCount } from 'ai';
import { z } from 'zod';

const { text, steps } = await generateText({
  model: 'openai/gpt-6-astra',
  stopWhen: isStepCount(5),
  tools: {
    weather: tool({
      description: 'Get the weather in a location',
      inputSchema: z.object({
        location: z.string().describe('The location to get the weather for'),
      }),
      execute: async ({ location }: { location: string }) => ({
        location,
        temperature: 72 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 21) - 10,
      }),
    }),
  },
  prompt: 'What is the weather in San Francisco?',
});
```

--------------------------------

### Stopping generation using isStepCount

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/07-reference/01-ai-sdk-core/70-is-step-count.mdx

Configure generateText to stop execution after reaching a set number of completed steps.

```ts
import { generateText, isStepCount } from 'ai';
__PROVIDER_IMPORT__;

const result = await generateText({
  model: __MODEL__,
  tools: {
    // your tools
  },
  // Stop after 5 steps
  stopWhen: isStepCount(5),
});
```

--------------------------------

### generateText tool calling loop (do/while pattern)

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/generate-text/generate-text.ts

The core tool-calling agent loop in generateText, which continues as long as all client tool calls have been executed, there are tools to process, and no stop condition is met. Default stop condition is `isStepCount(1)` (one step, no tool loop).

```typescript
      do {
        if (steps.length > 0) {
          mergedAbortSignal?.throwIfAborted();
        }

        const stepTimeoutId = setAbortTimeout({
          abortController: stepAbortController,
          label: 'Step',
          timeoutMs: stepTimeoutMs,
        });
        const stepNumber = steps.length;

        try {
          await runInTracingChannelSpan({
            type: 'step',
            event: { callId, stepNumber },
            execute: async () => {
              const accumulatedResponseMessages = [
                ...initialResponseMessages,
                ...steps.flatMap(step => step.response.messages),
              ];
              const stepInputMessages = messagesForNextStep;
              // ... step execution, model call, tool parsing, tool execution ...
            },
          });
        } finally {
          if (stepTimeoutId != null) {
            clearTimeout(stepTimeoutId);
          }
        }
      } while (
        // Continue only after all client tool calls have been executed or denied,
        // and if there are client results or pending deferred provider results.
        clientToolOutputs.length + deniedToolApprovalResponses.length ===
          clientToolCalls.length &&
        (clientToolCalls.length > 0 || pendingDeferredToolCalls.size > 0) &&
        // continue until a stop condition is met:
        !(await isStopConditionMet({ stopConditions, steps }))
      );
```

--------------------------------

### Combining tool calling with structured outputs using generateText

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/09-troubleshooting/14-tool-calling-with-structured-outputs.mdx

Adjust the stopWhen condition by adding at least 1 step to account for structured output generation alongside tool calls and tool results.

```tsx
const result = await generateText({
  model: __MODEL__,
  output: Output.object({
    schema: z.object({
      summary: z.string(),
      sentiment: z.enum(['positive', 'neutral', 'negative']),
    }),
  }),
  tools: {
    analyze: tool({
      description: 'Analyze data',
      inputSchema: z.object({
        data: z.string(),
      }),
      execute: async ({ data }) => {
        return { result: 'analyzed' };
      }),
    },
  },
  // Add at least 1 to your intended step count to account for structured output
  stopWhen: isStepCount(3), // Now accounts for: tool call + tool result + structured output
  prompt: 'Analyze the data and provide a summary',
});
```

